  data: {
    LLM: "Evaluate your hand for both high-trick potential and low-trick potential. A hand with many 7s and 8s is perfect for a Misère bid.\n\nAuction Tactics: Use the 'Preference' suit to overcall opponents even if your trick count is lower. Knowing when to 'Double' an opponent's contract is key to defensive scoring.\n\nDefensive Coordination: Since three players defend against one declarer, they must cooperate to force the declarer to win (in Misère) or lose (in Boston) tricks. Lead through the declarer to trap their high cards.",
